\underline{Remark} 1.14.  Let  $\underline{A}$  be a cofibered groupoid over  $\underline{C}_\wedge$  , admitting a minimally-versal formal object  $\xi$  . Then an invariant of  $R = P(\xi)$  , which is a complete local  $\wedge$-algebra of formally finite type over  $\wedge$  , is automatically an invariant of  $\underline{A}$  over  $\underline{C}_\wedge$  . Therefore, for example, we shall say that  $\underline{A}$  is (formally) smooth over  $\underline{C}_\wedge$  if  $R$  is (formally) smooth over  $\wedge$  i.e., a formal power-series algebra over  $\wedge$  , or we say that  $\underline{A}$  is irreducible over  $\underline{C}_\wedge$  if  $\mathrm{Spec}(R)$  is irreducible etc. In the next section we introduce the notion of  "smoothness"  of a functor  $\underline{A} \to \underline{B}$  over  $\underline{C}_\wedge$  , where  $\underline{A}, \underline{B}$  are cofibered categories in groupoids over  $\underline{C}_\wedge$  . It turns out (cf. 2.4) that  "$\underline{A}$  is (formally) smooth over  $\underline{C}_\wedge$"  is equivalent to  " $P : \underline{A} \to \underline{C}_\wedge$  is a smooth functor"  , and therefore no confusion arises. We also define the dimension of  $\underline{A}$  over  $\underline{C}_\wedge$  by  $\dim_{\underline{C}_\wedge} \underline{A} = \dim\, k \otimes_\wedge R$  . For this we note the following fact:  Let  $\underline{C}_k$  be the category of artinian local $k$-algebras with the same residue field  $k$  . Then  $\underline{C}_k \to \underline{C}_\wedge$  is a fully-faithful imbedding, whose (left) adjoint functor  $\underline{C}_\wedge \to \underline{C}_k$  is given by  $R \to k \otimes_\wedge R$  . Let $\underline{A}|\underline{C}_k$  be the pull-back of  $P : \underline{A} \to \underline{C}_\wedge$  under  $\underline{C}_k \to \underline{C}_\wedge$  . Then it is trivial to see that if  $\xi$  is a minimally-versal formal object for  $\underline{A}$  over  $\underline{C}_\wedge$  , then  $k \otimes_\wedge \xi$ is a mi