by the lines in $H^0(X,\mathcal O_X(d))$, that is, by
\begin{equation}\tag{1.3.1}
U=\mathbb P\bigl(H^0(X,\mathcal O_X(d)).
\end{equation}
Over $U$ we have the ``universal section of $X$ by a hypersurface of degree
